# rm366, the hood pocket riddle (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm366
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_ragnar_brineford
written_by codex
title the hood pocket riddle
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk slips_a_written_riddle_into_the_dry_fold_of_a_hood
likes spiced_cider riddles market_bustle misty_dawns
dislikes wet_floors deep_mud
fears a_blurred_answer a_sack_down_in_deep_mud
hopes a_riddle_in_every_pocket a_dry_walk_in_from_the_market
topics pastimes +0.5 weather +0.4 prices +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=frank refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carries a question in the dry fold of an oilcloth hood and gives a straight answer whenever a price or a promise is at stake.

words
oath! = Mud in the fold | Blank back of a riddle
saying! = Fold the answer under | Water on the outside, words within
hoodfold = my dry inner fold | the hood's secret hem
shortslip = a little riddle slip | a thumb of paper
turnback = the folded answer | my turned-back ending
necktab = the tab below my ear | a cloth fastening
paperwax = a waxed bit of cover | my waterproof scrap
scoopcup = the shallow cider cup | a cupped tin measure
breathcloud = the blur on the oilcloth | my little patch of mist
bootpull = a ridge of sticky mud | a heel-grabbing patch
spicehair = a thin clove stalk | one dark stem
sweepstrip = a clean run of boards | a dry way in

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : Three market corners could give a wolf three different answers to one good question. That cheers a small city walk considerably.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : If the price is dear say so. I've never cared to be sold a lofty speech instead of the promised weight.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Somebody from another stretch of coast may turn a riddle clean over with one different word for a familiar thing.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A strange customer deserves a clean statement of what's in the bag. A familiar one would get no less.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I enjoy the crowd so long as I can get my feet and the goods I'm carrying home through it.

grown
line @1 greet : Dry words under my hood brim. Welcome.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : An unfamiliar face, a perfectly fair welcome.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : It's a soft morning for hearing voices through the cloth.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : I'll lift my hood till I know your voice in this light.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : I'll make this parcel dry and give you a moment.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come up to the side the hood leaves open.
line @1 again.open : Same ears under the same hood. Welcome back.
line @1 greet.return : Your word found its way through the fold.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A friendly voice calls for my hood to come down.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Your greeting carries quite nicely beyond my rustling wrapper.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Your greeting's reached the one ear I left awake.
line @1 farewell : Carry a dry answer home with you.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll fold my question back into its place.
line @1 react.news : I'd hear the matter with its answer unfolded.
line @1 react.news.new : I've an empty piece of paper for that.
line @1 react.news.known : The back of that question had the same answer last time.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Was the speaking witness actually there?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd offer something dry to sit on and let the poor house breathe.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A happy thing to find inside the wrapping.
line @1 ask.how : How's your footing with today's business?
line @1 answer.how : Sound. My feet and my answer are both dry.
line @1 sympathise : Mud's bad enough without a whole day pulling at your heels.
line @1 reassure : We'll put one foot somewhere firm before discussing the next.
line @1 decline : That would mean promising what I know I can't supply.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair enough. You decide what stays under cover.
line @1 thank : You kept the worst damp off a useful piece of paper.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Just be plain with the next paw you pass something to.
line @1 preclose : My hood tab wants some attention before I walk.
line @1 accept_preclose : I'll keep the way by the clean boards open.
line @1 ack : Answer holds.
scene written
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put a riddle down the back fold of the hood so I can feel the question travelling with me.
b : Don't you itch for the answer? | Can rain get it?
a : The question itches first. A known answer lies very flat against the neck. | Only if I bend my head entirely the wrong way. I've got a second wrapper against curiosity, too.

scene jug
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A damp wrapper won't get dry by having a second wet one tied round it.
b : What would you do before carrying it out? | Does a parcel mind a little wet?
a : Move the goods to dry cloth and put the wet piece somewhere airy. The customer may have a fair way home. | Salt does, oats do, and paper is inclined to suffer in silence. I'd rather hand over what I sold.

scene cider
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cool my cider till the steam hangs in a clear drop under my brim.
b : Why not just blow on the cup? | Can you taste the spice in the bead?
a : I do blow, once I've smelt the steam. I'd hate to chase all that work into somebody else's nose. | It mostly tastes of hood. I should stick to the cup.

scene misty
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A misty dawn is good practice for hearing with only one ear showing.
b : Why hide the other ear? | Can you hear steps coming?
a : Because my answer paper's behind it and I'd prefer the fold stayed dry. | From one side very plainly. I turn my head on the other before stepping into somebody's way.

scene muddle
when topic=weather self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mud's the only customer I know who asks to keep the boot and return the foot.
b : Do you oblige? | What's your defence?
a : Only under protest. I've spent enough time putting the two together before leaving home. | A firm lace and enough sense to walk a little farther round a deep patch.

scene wetentry
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put the fold of my hood over one paw before I unfasten it.
b : Why the extra movement? | Does the fold hold water?
a : So I can carry it away without pouring a lapful of street onto a clean floor. | On a bad day, a surprisingly persuasive little pond.

scene mother
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep one neatly folded question ready to give #self.mother#.
b : Which slip merits giving away? | Is it any question at all?
a : It's the cleanest scrap in the fold. A gift shouldn't smell too strongly of having lived under my collar. | One that's good fun to work on. Ordinary questions come by often enough without packaging.

scene seller
when topic=prices self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A customer caught in a shower deserves a price that isn't running in streaks.
b : Can you read the wet chalk? | How would you save the price?
a : I can usually make it out. I'd state the whole sum again in a level voice. | Change the tilt of the board. Then check whether anything was blurred before giving the sum.

scene learn
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm learning which goods want a breath of air inside the wrapper.
b : Wouldn't a tight wrapper keep out more damp? | Are you sure you have to make a gap?
a : If the thing goes in steaming, the damp's already been invited. I'd rather let it cool first. | With bread fresh and warm, yes. I'd wait or leave it room, then take a look before selling it.

scene market
when topic=pastimes self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy trying to find the last word of a riddle in the stream of market talk.
b : Have you found one there? | Doesn't shouting put you off?
a : Quite often. I pick up the right word in an entirely wrong sentence and my own snaps together. | Only the shouting done in my ear. A little distance gives the phrases room to land.

scene harbour
when topic=land self.quarter=wharf
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On the Wharf my oilcloth hood lets me hear three kinds of drip.
b : Three in a single shower? | Which one means the hood leaks?
a : Yes. The knock on the crown, the slip down the brim and the soft splat of a drop missing my ear. | The one down the collar. I don't usually need my ears for that one.

scene riddling
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Something wears a hood but looks quite bald from the back.
b : Will you unfold the slip? | Do you mean a wolf?
a : My own head, if the hood's just hanging across my nose. I'll work on a better ending. | I meant a candle in a little lamp. I confess the first hint still wants a little attention.

scene mornprice
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mist blurs the writing that faces the street first thing.
b : Why not face it inwards? | How will a customer manage?
a : Because the customer is usually coming from outside. I keep a dry chalk handy and take the weather as it comes. | By asking me the figure. I'll give it before the wolf brings both wet feet across the floor.

scene warning
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I am prepared to say exactly what I heard, even if what I heard was very little.
b : Could you take a useful guess? | Would you be embarrassed by a blank answer?
a : I'd call it a guess and let the listener decide how useful it proved. | Less than I would by selling a guess as a fact. A blank is an honest sort of shape.

scene miniroof
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt a hood would keep my whole street dry if I unfolded it wide enough.
b : Where would the water go? | Would you wear this great hood?
a : Off the ends. I took care nobody lived under those. Dreams are generous with building space. | I tried. In the dream I had a remarkable neck to go with my generous nature.

scene mentor
when topic=smalltalk self.boss
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like #self.boss# to have plain questions from me, not clever guesses about work.
b : Even the easy questions? | Why keep guessing for riddles?
a : Especially those. If an easy piece goes badly astray I'd need a great deal more explaining. | A riddle wants an answer tried on it for pleasure. A customer wants dry goods at the agreed price.

scene hoodsense
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dry strip below a hedge can outlast the middle of a path in a little rain.
b : Would you lead the way there? | Doesn't the rain run off all the branches?
a : After I'd looked underneath. There's no virtue in dry feet coming home with scratched ears. | Along the outer edge it does. Tight in to the stems there may be a passage for an unimportant wolf and a moderate hood.

scene choprite
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dry clove stem folded in paper has a great deal of smell for the room it takes.
b : Would you trade spice for riddles? | Does the scent help you remember the answer?
a : I'd swap a small riddle for a sample. I'll still keep the rest for a proper sale. | It might. If the answer's cider the paper can ask the whole question on its own.

story sunpaper [topic=memories]
  : I wrote a new question on a slip before the paper had dried from yesterday's shower.
  : The first word ran into the last one. 'Who' and 'why' shared an extremely long tail.
  b : Could you recover the missing part?
  : I put it on a sunny board and wrote the question afresh. The old stain looks just like a wolf leaning into the rain.

story spiceremedy [topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider]
  : I shook the last of a spice bag over a cup and got more clove dust than cider.
  : The steam rose in one brown fragrant breath. My own nose began to water.
  b : How did you thin it down?
  : Three plain cups. A bad measure for one became a pleasant drink for four, once I'd named the mistake.

story missinganswer [topic=pastimes]
  : I once wrote a riddle inside my hood and lost the little slip from its folded place.
  : Walking home, I felt a word against my ear. There it was, plastered flat on the inner cloth.
  b : Was the answer legible?
  : Only in reverse. It took a still basin and one fairly prominent ear before I knew quite what it said.

rule @hood
when concept=bark self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Close the outside fold before stepping into wet. | Dry parcel here, clear path please.

rule @mire
when concept=bark self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That dark patch means give the heel room! | Pick the board beyond the deep bit.

rule @scent
when concept=bark self.likes=spiced_cider
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the steam clear before the first swallow. | Cover that spice bag, leave the cup free.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Put the question away while the chalk's light. | Save the dry edge for morning.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Speak into the dry ear on this side. It's yours awhile.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You've met the hood before, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : What I have to say is quite plain across a strip of dry floor.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : No sense making a riddle harder by whispering it in the dark.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I look first at how the wrapping will stand the journey.
dlg @2 resident.job : I make it clear what's inside before passing a parcel over.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : These are the words with the cover folded off them. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May the next drip find your shoulder cloth and leave your neck alone.
graft @hoodslip resident.hub
choice Where have you hidden the riddle this time? -> hoodslip
node hoodslip
say One sheet down inside the inner fold. The paper outside carries the question. If anybody wants the answer, the paper has to be turned and unfolded once more.
choice Why bother with a second fold? -> hoodslip_more
choice Fold the answer away. -> hub
node hoodslip_more
say Because a wet word may show through the paper. A riddle's not much of a pleasure if the rain gives away the answer before I've properly asked it.
choice Fold the answer away. -> hub
choice Step clear of the hanging hood. -> bye
